  claude: "`[MODEL]` defaults to the model that reliably handles most package work. Escalate to the strongest available model — either the package worker itself, or a one-off task dispatch per `<dispatch>` — only for system-level or cross-cutting work where early decisions shape the rest, never as the roster default. A lighter, cheaper model fits a package that is bounded, low-ambiguity, single-component work.\n",
  codex: "`[EFFORT]` defaults to `standard` — the tier that reliably handles most package work. Escalate to `deep` — either the package worker itself, or a one-off task dispatch per `<dispatch>` — only for system-level or cross-cutting work where early decisions shape the rest, never as the roster default. `light` fits a package that is bounded, low-ambiguity, single-component work.\n",
